========================================================================================
THE OPERATIVE CHANNEL  (n = 1,175 chemicals with >= 5 species)
========================================================================================
  rho(HC5, log records ) = -0.1558   p = 8.01e-08
  rho(HC5, log species ) = -0.2411   p = 5.31e-17

  partial(species, HC5 | records) = -0.2054  p = 1.17e-12   <- survives
  partial(records, HC5 | species) = +0.0881  p = 0.00252   <- SIGN REVERSES
  A single latent effort factor measured with differential error would
  attenuate both partials; it cannot reverse one.  The reversal is
  produced by estimator structure, and is predicted a priori:
    partial(replication depth, sd  | species) = -0.1223  p = 2.63e-05
    partial(replication depth, mu  | species) = +0.0484  p = 0.0974
    partial(replication depth, HC5 | species) = +0.0980  p = 0.000764
  i.e. replication within species shrinks the between-species SD
  estimate, which RAISES the HC5 -- the opposite sign to adding species.

========================================================================================
F-STRAT: the three-stratum table does not reproduce; use pooled partials
========================================================================================
  hand-chosen strata, for the record (cut-point dependent):
    [5-7] n=481 rho=+0.057 p=0.215 | [8-14] n=337 rho=+0.184 p=0.001 | [15-+] n=357 rho=-0.174 p=0.001
    [5-6] n=366 rho=+0.040 p=0.446 | [7-10] n=320 rho=+0.192 p=0.001 | [11-+] n=489 rho=-0.166 p=0.000
  -> significant in two of three with OPPOSITE signs.  Not publishable.

  pooled over 18 exact-species-count strata (n >= 10 each):
    rho(records, HC5 | species) = +0.1161  95% CI [+0.052, +0.179]
  species effect within record-count quartiles: -0.149, -0.146, -0.118, -0.331
    pooled rho(species, HC5 | records) = -0.1873  95% CI [-0.242, -0.131]   <- survives in every stratum

========================================================================================
F-DECOMP: what the species slope is made of
========================================================================================
  between-chemical slope, HC5 ~ log10(species) : -1.2084 per decade
    after c4 small-sample SD correction        : -1.1516   -> c4 explains 4.7%
    within-chemical rarefaction (235 chemicals >= 20 species,
      chemical fixed effects, 60 draws at s = 5/8/12/20)
      slope = -0.1626 (se 0.0108)   -> estimator sample size = 13.5%
        mean rarefied HC5 at s =  5 : -1.5838
        mean rarefied HC5 at s = 20 : -1.6785
      a shorter species list gives a HIGHER HC5 -- data-poor substances
      are UNDER-protected, and c4 fixes only a twentieth of it.
    restricted to the  50 most-tested species (n =  805) : rho = -0.2367, partial | records = -0.1242
    restricted to the 100 most-tested species (n =  950) : rho = -0.2055, partial | records = -0.1471
    restricted to the 200 most-tested species (n = 1048) : rho = -0.2171, partial | records = -0.1357
      -> species-pool composition explains essentially none of it.

========================================================================================
F-MED: restoring the hazard-attention statement with a LEGITIMATE control
========================================================================================
  40 independent splits, n = 1,214 chemicals with >= 10 records
    total rho(depth-equalised minimum, log n)      -0.1609  split sd 0.0063
    partial | held-out within-chemical SD (mediator) -0.0284  split sd 0.0137
    partial | held-out hazard level  (legitimate)   -0.1014  split sd 0.0206   95% CI [-0.158, -0.045]
    the legitimate control leaves 63% of the total.
  Conditioning on within-chemical SD conditions on a descendant of
  effort, so the near-zero partial understates the direct effect.

  F-FILL: rho(log n, within-chemical SD)
    with fillna(0) over 1,266 singleton chemicals (26.6% of 4,757) : +0.7829   <- as published
    on n >= 5, no imputation (n = 1,977)            : +0.3312   <- correct
    on n >= 2, no imputation (n = 3,491)            : +0.4759

